SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia (15 August)\, Glossa and Loutraki
LOCATION:Glossa / Loutraki\, Skopelos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The north of the island celebrates Dekapentavgoustos twice over: the municipality's panigiri on the little harbour of Loutraki (15 August in 2025\, the 16th in 2026\, with a local singer and dancing by the water)\, and since 2025 a revived all-night glenti in the central square of Glossa village above it\, where the music went on until 6 am. Between them there is a shuttle-worthy 3 km of hairpins\, so decide where you will sleep\; rooms in Glossa are few and go early in August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#glossa-loutraki-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-glossa-and-lou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skopelos/#glossa-loutraki-panigiri-of-panagia-15-august-glossa-and-lou
END:VEVENT
